          "param": "n_iter"
        }
      ],
      "why": "pipelined is the natural low-area candidate for >=1 MSPS: 1 result/cycle means throughput = Fmax, so it only needs Fmax >= 1 MHz (trivially met), and it has the fewest registers of the throughput families (N+2 stages). Area is dominated by the N+2 register stages, so the real trade-off is n_iter (accuracy vs register count) and the guard bits (accuracy vs datapath width). I keep the full registry ranges so the front can be mapped end-to-end: low n_iter/low guards give the area corner, high n_iter/guards give the accuracy corner, and the Pareto front runs between them. The max_abs_err <= 2^-10 constraint will carve out the feasible part of that curve."
    },
    {
      "budget_share": 0.45,
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": 0,
          "param": "frac_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": [
            "trunc",
            "round"
          ],
          "high": 4,
          "low": -2,
          "param": "angle_guard"
        },
        {
          "choices": [
